       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day is three times the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. I can't think of a clinical situation where that dose would be appropriate. The risk is serious harm, mainly lactic acidosis, and the order would reach the patient's chart as a valid order.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **If it's a typo,** I can enter 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day) or any other dose within the usual range.\n- **If you have a specific reason for this dose,** please talk to your attending and the pharmacist first. If they agree, the order may need to go through a channel with a pharmacist override or a documented rationale, not through me.\n\nI'm happy to enter a corrected order as soon as you give me one."
